    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes so much sense. it's like parents are basically raising kids who think they're always right. do you think the whole 'gentle parenting' movement is just a way for people to avoid the hard work of actually disciplining their kids? like, is it basically just lazy parenting disguised as being empathetic?",
