      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Many critics argue that the emphasis on \"being nice\" can become a form of avoidance, allowing parents to sidestep the difficult but necessary work of conflict resolution and consistent enforcement. From this perspective, it can be seen as prioritizing parental comfort and immediate emotional peace over the child's long-term behavioral development. Viewpoint suggests that genuine empathy must be balanced with parental responsibility to set and uphold appropriate limits. Therefore, while framed as compassionate, some see it as an abdication of the fundamental role of guiding and training a child through necessary friction.",
